From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:53:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] droidcamsrc: close the camera outside the device lock

droid_media_camera_disconnect() is being made to wait for camera
callbacks that are still running before it frees the camera, so that a
callback can no longer run on a freed DroidMediaCamera (droidmedia
branch luneos/teardown-races, not sent upstream yet). Those callbacks
take dev->lock, and dev_close() called disconnect with dev->lock held,
which would make the wait run into its timeout.

Take the camera out of dev under the lock and disconnect it after
unlocking. dev->cam is NULL by then, so a callback that runs during the
disconnect sees a closed camera: dev_start() (which a late JPEG calls to
restart the preview) now fails on it instead of using a NULL camera, and
the recording frame release paths skip the release, which downstream
can also reach after the close when it still holds a frame.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c b/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c
index 66cb70c..1437f1c 100644
--- a/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c
+++ b/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrcdev.c
@@ -367,7 +367,8 @@ gst_droidcamsrc_dev_video_frame_callback (void *user,
   /* unlikely but just in case */
   if (G_UNLIKELY (!data)) {
     GST_ERROR ("invalid memory from camera HAL");
-    droid_media_camera_release_recording_frame (dev->cam, video_data);
+    if (dev->cam)
+      droid_media_camera_release_recording_frame (dev->cam, video_data);
     goto unlock_and_out;
   }
 
@@ -667,17 +668,22 @@ gst_droidcamsrc_dev_open (GstDroidCamSrcDev * dev, GstDroidCamSrcCamInfo * info)
 void
 gst_droidcamsrc_dev_close (GstDroidCamSrcDev * dev)
 {
+  DroidMediaCamera *cam;
+
   GST_DEBUG ("dev close");
 
   g_rec_mutex_lock (dev->lock);
+  cam = dev->cam;
+  dev->cam = NULL;
+  dev->queue = NULL;
+  g_rec_mutex_unlock (dev->lock);
 
-  if (dev->cam) {
-    droid_media_camera_disconnect (dev->cam);
-    dev->cam = NULL;
-    dev->queue = NULL;
+  /* Not under dev->lock: droidmedia waits for camera callbacks that are
+   * still running before it frees the camera, and those take dev->lock.
+   * dev->cam is already NULL for any of them that look. */
+  if (cam) {
+    droid_media_camera_disconnect (cam);
   }
-
-  g_rec_mutex_unlock (dev->lock);
 }
 
 void
@@ -784,6 +790,11 @@ gst_droidcamsrc_dev_start (GstDroidCamSrcDev * dev, gboolean apply_settings)
     goto out;
   }
 
+  if (!dev->cam) {
+    GST_WARNING_OBJECT (src, "camera is closed");
+    goto out;
+  }
+
   GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (src, "dev start");
 
   if (!dev->use_raw_data) {
@@ -1125,7 +1136,9 @@ gst_droidcamsrc_dev_release_recording_frame (void *data,
   g_rec_mutex_lock (dev->lock);
   --dev->vid->queued_frames;
 
-  droid_media_camera_release_recording_frame (dev->cam, video_data->data);
+  /* downstream can hold a frame past the close of the camera */
+  if (dev->cam)
+    droid_media_camera_release_recording_frame (dev->cam, video_data->data);
 
   g_slice_free (GstDroidCamSrcDevVideoData, video_data);
   g_rec_mutex_unlock (dev->lock);
-- 
2.53.0

